    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0808" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/3244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-21T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4.40 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5355. Your 4110,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d650-f1"/> December 1, 7 p. m. and
                        4144,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d650-f2"/> December 7, 6 p. m. In support of the
                    original request contained in your 4048,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d650-f3"/>
                    November 16, 3 p. m., which was answered by Foreign Office in the sense of my
                    5272 [5271?],<anchor n="3" xml:id="d650-f4"/> December 5, 5 p. m., renewed
                    representations based on your above instructions were presented. Foreign Office
                    replies in note received to-day that the concession made upon my request and
                    contained in my note quoted in my 5076,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d650-f5"/> October
                    26, was intended to operate in substitution for previous arrangements and that
                    in these circumstances it regrets its inability to accede to the request based
                    on your 4110, December 1, 7 p. m., and 4144, December 7, 6 p. m.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d650-f6"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
